orm part of a 789 chow in Characters and conflicts with the knitted assignment (where Characters is 1,4,7, making W9 irrelevant). Other options like B2 or B8 offer more chow flexibility (e.g., B2 for 123/234, B8 for 678/789), while honors (e.g., F3, J3) could contribute to wind/dragon patterns but are less critical early on. Discarding W9 avoids cluttering the hand with low-potential terminals and aligns with standard early-game strategy of shedding inflexible tiles.\n\nReason: Knitted Straight is achievable and scores 12 points (above the 8-point minimum), with my current holdings providing a solid base. Keeping W9 hinders this path, as it cannot integrate into the knitted structure and limits drawing opportunities for missing knitted tiles (W4, W7, T5, T8, B9). Discarding it now streamlines the hand toward a high-probability winning pattern without sacrificing key components.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
